<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:conv="using:DotCharter.Tone.UI.Converters"
        xmlns:fire="clr-namespace:DotCharter.Tone.UI.Controls.Fire;assembly=DotCharter.Tone.UI">

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         THE "FIRE" DESIGN LAYER — component half.
         Tokens: Styles/FireTokens.axaml.  Written up: docs/agents/ui/fire-design-system.md.

         Every class here is prefixed `Fire`. That is not decoration: the app
         already has THREE partly-overlapping grammars using bare names
         (`Eyebrow`, `StatTile`, `GlassPanel`, … in PlayModeView / ShellStyles /
         BoardStyles). A bare `Eyebrow` here would silently re-style all of them
         the moment a Fire surface was hosted inside the Play Mode shell.

         WHAT A FIRE SCREEN IS MADE OF (this is the whole vocabulary):

            ground   Border.FireGround (+ .Screen) with a Border.FireWash on top
            screen   Border.FireScreen        a floating modal, radius 18
            regions  Border.FireRail | FireContextRail | FireHeader | FireFooter
            surfaces Border.FirePanel | FireCard | FireHeroPanel
            lockup   TextBlock.FireEyebrow over TextBlock.FireScreenTitle/FireTitle
            rows     FireNavRowButton/Toggle — 3 px accent bar + title + desc
                                                       (+ an optional trailing badge)
            state    Border.FireStatusPill (.Success/.Warn/.Danger/.Accent)
                                            = Border.FireDot + TextBlock.FireStatusText
            figures  TextBlock.FireFigure over TextBlock.FireStatLabel
            actions  Button.FireCta > Button.FirePrimary > Button.FireGhost > Button.FireQuiet
            inputs   Border.FireField, Border.FireSegment/FireSegmentItem,
                     ToggleSwitch Theme={FireToggleSwitch}
            marks    Border.FireTag/.FireBadge/.FireChip, Border.FireTrack/FireTrackFill

         TWO HOUSE RULES THIS FILE OBEYS, AND SO MUST ANY ADDITION:

         • NO `Transitions` SETTER. Building an `AvaloniaList<ITransition>`
           calls `Dispatcher.VerifyAccess`, which makes the whole dictionary
           UI-thread-only — the trap that took out all nine `SettingsSearchTests`
           in 0.35 — and every Fire surface so far is an `IsVisible`-gated one
           whose style clocks would keep ticking while hidden. The mockups'
           `transition: all .16s ease` is therefore deliberately NOT ported;
           hover is instant, like the rest of this app's shell.
         • ACCENT IS INFORMATION. The 3 px bar, one primary action per surface,
           and a status colour are the sanctioned uses. A row of equally
           accent-tinted cards says nothing.
         • EVERY INTERACTIVE CONTROL HAS HOVER, FOCUS **AND** DISABLED. The
           menu is keyboard and controller navigable, so a control you can
           reach with Tab and cannot SEE is a defect, not a polish item. Focus
           is a 2 px `FireAccentPale` ring offset outside the control
           (`FocusAdornerTemplate`) on anything button-shaped, and a violet
           tint + border on a list row, where a ring around a full-width row
           would read as a second selection.
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

    <Styles.Resources>

        <!-- The primary action's CHAMFER. Bound to the button's live Bounds so
             the 45° cut off its top-right and bottom-left corners stays a
             constant 16 px at every size — see the converter's own notes for
             why a static geometry cannot do this. -->
        <conv:FireChamferClipConverter x:Key="FireChamferClip" />

        <!-- ─── ToggleSwitch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
             A 44×24 accent pill with a lit track and a white knob. A
             `TemplatedControl` gets its template from a `ControlTheme`, never
             from a `Style` with a `Template` setter (`KeybindCaptureBox` lived
             as the latter for four releases and rendered as an empty column).
             Keyed rather than type-keyed so it stays opt-in: a surface asks for
             it with `Theme="{DynamicResource FireToggleSwitch}"` and every other
             ToggleSwitch in the app keeps the Fluent-derived look. -->
        <ControlTheme x:Key="FireToggleSwitch" TargetType="ToggleSwitch">
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="OnContent" Value="" />
            <Setter Property="OffContent" Value="" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Right" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <!-- `PART_MovingKnobs` is a REQUIRED template part on
                         Avalonia's ToggleSwitch (AVLN2205 at build time if it
                         is missing) and it must be a Panel — the built-in
                         knob transition animates its RenderTransform. This
                         template positions the knob by alignment instead, so
                         the panel is a pass-through wrapper. -->
                    <Border x:Name="PART_Track"
                            Width="44" Height="24"
                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusPill}"
                            Background="{DynamicResource SurfaceElevated}"
                            BorderThickness="{StaticResource FireBorderHairline}"
                            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource FireBorderStrong}">
                        <Panel x:Name="PART_SwitchKnob">
                            <Panel x:Name="PART_MovingKnobs">
                                <Border x:Name="PART_Knob"
                                        Width="18" Height="18"
                                        Margin="2,0,0,0"
                                        CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusPill}"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                        Background="{DynamicResource FireTextDim}" />
                            </Panel>
                        </Panel>
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <!-- Graphite: ON is the one accent, flat — no second blue, no glow —
                 and the knob is dark ink so it reads against the light track. -->
            <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ Border#PART_Track">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccent}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccent}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ Border#PART_Knob">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextOnAccent}" />
                <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Right" />
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,2,0" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover /template/ Border#PART_Track">
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentBorderSoft}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.45" />
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>

        <!-- ─── …and the popover's 38 × 21 version ───────────────────────────
             `Play Menus.dc.html`'s PLAY STYLE row: `width:38; height:21;
             padding:2; radius:999`, an unlit track of `rgba(255,255,255,.1)`,
             a `linear-gradient(100deg,#3c7bd1,#5e9ff2)` when on, and a 17 px
             white knob under `0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.5)`.

             A separate theme rather than size setters on the one above, because
             the TRACK and KNOB sizes are literals inside a `ControlTemplate` and
             a setter on the control cannot reach them. It also carries NO
             `BoxShadow` on the track: the 44 px switch lights a settings row,
             this one sits 13 px from a popup's edge, where a feather falls
             outside the presenter and renders flat black. -->
        <ControlTheme x:Key="FirePopoverSwitch" TargetType="ToggleSwitch">
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="OnContent" Value="" />
            <Setter Property="OffContent" Value="" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Right" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border x:Name="PART_Track"
                            Width="{StaticResource FirePopoverSwitchWidth}"
                            Height="{StaticResource FirePopoverSwitchHeight}"
                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusPill}"
                            Background="{DynamicResource FireSurfaceTrack}">
                        <!-- `PART_MovingKnobs` is a REQUIRED part (AVLN2205 at
                             build time without it) and must be a Panel — the
                             built-in transition animates its RenderTransform.
                             This template positions by alignment instead, so it
                             is a pass-through wrapper. -->
                        <Panel x:Name="PART_SwitchKnob">
                            <Panel x:Name="PART_MovingKnobs">
                                <Border x:Name="PART_Knob"
                                        Width="{StaticResource FirePopoverSwitchKnob}"
                                        Height="{StaticResource FirePopoverSwitchKnob}"
                                        Margin="2,0,0,0"
                                        CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusPill}"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                        Background="{DynamicResource FireTextBright}" />
                            </Panel>
                        </Panel>
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ Border#PART_Track">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FirePopoverAccentAction}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ Border#PART_Knob">
                <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Right" />
                <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,2,0" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.45" />
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>

        <!-- ─── Nav row ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
             THE signature component: a 3 px accent bar, a title over a
             description, and an optional trailing badge. Selected = accent
             tint + accent border + the bar lit and glowing.

             It exists twice on purpose — as a `ToggleButton` (a rail whose
             selection is state, e.g. the settings tabs) and as a `Button` (a
             menu whose entries are destinations). Same template, so the two
             cannot drift; `^` selectors inside a ControlTheme keep each one's
             states with its own theme.

             THE BAR IS THERE AT REST. The spec is explicit — "transparent at
             rest with a 3 px violet-DIM indicator bar" — and the toggle
             variant used to paint it `Transparent`, so a rail of unselected
             rows had no left edge at all and the selected row's bar read as
             decoration rather than as a position in a list.

             HOVER SLIDES 3 px RIGHT (`translateX(3px)`, spec). It is a
             `RenderTransform`, applied instantly: this file may never carry a
             `Transitions` setter, so the motion token exists for the
             custom-drawn controls and not for this. -->
        <ControlTheme x:Key="FireNavRowToggle" TargetType="ToggleButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource FireRadiusRow}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="{StaticResource FirePadRow}" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="{StaticResource FireGapNavRow}" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
            <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translateX(0px)" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border x:CompileBindings="False"
                            Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                            BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                            CornerRadius="{Binding CornerRadius, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}">
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceLg}"
                              Margin="{Binding Padding, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}">
                            <Border x:Name="Bar" Grid.Column="0"
                                    Width="{StaticResource FireBarWidth}"
                                    Height="{StaticResource FireBarHeight}"
                                    CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusBar}"
                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                    Background="{DynamicResource FireAccentBar}" />
                            <ContentPresenter Grid.Column="1"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                              VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Grid>
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Setter Property="FocusAdorner">
                <FocusAdornerTemplate>
                    <Border BorderBrush="{DynamicResource FireFocusRowBorder}"
                            BorderThickness="{StaticResource FireBorderHairline}"
                            Background="{DynamicResource FireFocusRowFill}"
                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusRow}" />
                </FocusAdornerTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentTintSoft}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentBorderSoft}" />
                <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translateX(3px)" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover /template/ Border#Bar">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccent}" />
                <Setter Property="BoxShadow" Value="{DynamicResource FireGlowAccent}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:checked">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentTint}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentBorder}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:checked /template/ Border#Bar">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccent}" />
                <Setter Property="BoxShadow" Value="{DynamicResource FireGlowAccent}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.45" />
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>

        <!-- ─── Choice chip ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
             ONE option of a multi-select cluster, as a real `ToggleButton`
             rather than a Border. The mockups draw the planner's pillar cards
             and its MON–SUN day strip as tinted outlined boxes with no checkbox
             in sight, and nothing here covered that: `FireTag` is decoration,
             `FireSegmentItem` is a Border inside a single-SELECT frame, and
             `FireNavRow` is a rail row with a 3 px bar. Any of them would have
             rendered right and toggled nothing — the exact fault design 6's
             practice queue shipped with. -->
        <ControlTheme x:Key="FireChoiceToggle" TargetType="ToggleButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireSurfaceCard}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource FireBorderStrong}" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource FireRadiusRow}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="{StaticResource FirePadSegmentItem}" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="{StaticResource FireFieldHeight}" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FireFontMono}" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{StaticResource FireSizeXs}" />
            <Setter Property="LetterSpacing" Value="{StaticResource FireTrackStatus}" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextDim}" />
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <!-- CornerRadius is template-bound so a row used as a CARD
                         (the online hub's two offline destinations) can round
                         itself; the default stays 0, which is what a row in a
                         list wants. -->
                    <Border x:CompileBindings="False"
                            Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                            BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                            CornerRadius="{Binding CornerRadius, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}">
                        <ContentPresenter Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                          Margin="{Binding Padding, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}"
                                          HorizontalAlignment="{Binding HorizontalContentAlignment, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}"
                                          VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                          TextElement.Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" />
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover">
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentBorderSoft}" />
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextBody}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:checked">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentTint}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentBorder}" />
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextBright}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.45" />
            </Style>
            <Setter Property="FocusAdorner">
                <FocusAdornerTemplate>
                    <Border BorderBrush="{DynamicResource FireAccentPale}"
                            BorderThickness="{StaticResource FireFocusRingThickness}"
                            Margin="{StaticResource FireFocusRingOffset}"
                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusControl}" />
                </FocusAdornerTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <!-- The taller card form: the planner's four pillars, which carry a caption
                 over a description instead of one word. -->
            <Style Selector="^.FireChoice.Card">
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="{StaticResource FirePadCard}" />
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource FireRadiusControl}" />
                <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>

        <ControlTheme x:Key="FireNavRowButton" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource FireRadiusControl}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="{StaticResource FirePadRow}" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="{StaticResource FireGapNavRow}" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
            <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translateX(0px)" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border x:CompileBindings="False"
                            Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                            BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                            CornerRadius="{Binding CornerRadius, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}">
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="{StaticResource FireSpaceLg}"
                              Margin="{Binding Padding, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}">
                            <Border x:Name="Bar" Grid.Column="0"
                                    Width="{StaticResource FireBarWidth}"
                                    Height="{StaticResource FireBarHeightTall}"
                                    CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusBar}"
                                    VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                    Background="{DynamicResource FireAccentBar}" />
                            <ContentPresenter Grid.Column="1"
                                              Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                              VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Grid>
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Setter Property="FocusAdorner">
                <FocusAdornerTemplate>
                    <Border BorderBrush="{DynamicResource FireFocusRowBorder}"
                            BorderThickness="{StaticResource FireBorderHairline}"
                            Background="{DynamicResource FireFocusRowFill}"
                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusControl}" />
                </FocusAdornerTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentTintSoft}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentBorderSoft}" />
                <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translateX(3px)" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover /template/ Border#Bar">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccent}" />
                <Setter Property="BoxShadow" Value="{DynamicResource FireGlowAccent}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:pressed">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentTint}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentBorder}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.45" />
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>

        <!-- ─── The two LIT actions ──────────────────────────────────────────
             `BoxShadow` lives on `Border`, not on `Control`, so a Button style
             cannot set it (AVLN2000 at build time). A glowing button therefore
             needs a template whose root IS a Border — which is the whole reason
             these two own their TEMPLATE, where `FireGhost`/`FireQuiet`/`FireBack`
             (no glow) are class-gated rules over Fluent's (every button family is
             a ControlTheme since #240; those three live in Fire/FireActions.axaml).

             THE SILHOUETTE IS A CHAMFER, NOT A RADIUS. The mockups cut 12-18 px
             off the TOP-RIGHT and BOTTOM-LEFT corners with a `clip-path`
             polygon; it is a brand signature and the spec says so in as many
             words ("keep it"). The first port rounded those two corners hard
             instead (`FireRadiusCut = 0,16,0,16`), which reads as a lozenge.
             It is now a real `Clip`, produced from the button's live Bounds by
             `FireChamferClipConverter` so the notch is a constant 16 px
             whatever the button's size.

             THE STRUCTURE THAT FOLLOWS FROM THAT: `Clip` cuts an element's own
             rendering, INCLUDING its box shadow. So the glow lives on an outer
             Border that is NOT clipped, and the clipped fill is its child. The
             outer Border is `Transparent` on purpose — a fill there would show
             through the two notches. (Avalonia draws a box shadow whenever one
             is set, regardless of the background brush.) -->
        <ControlTheme x:Key="FireCtaButton" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentActionHero}" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextOnAccent}" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="{StaticResource FireCtaHeight}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="28,0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
            <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translateY(0px)" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border x:CompileBindings="False"
                            Background="Transparent"
                            BoxShadow="{DynamicResource FireGlowAction}">
                        <Border x:Name="Cut"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusControl}"
                                fire:FireShape.CutSize="{StaticResource FireCutSize}">
                            <Border.Clip>
                                <!-- bounds AND the theme's cut: a converter parameter is a
                                     plain value, so the token has to arrive as a binding. -->
                                <MultiBinding Converter="{StaticResource FireChamferClip}">
                                    <Binding ElementName="Cut" Path="Bounds" />
                                    <Binding ElementName="Cut" Path="(fire:FireShape.CutSize)" />
                                </MultiBinding>
                            </Border.Clip>
                            <Border x:Name="Sheen" Background="Transparent">
                                <ContentPresenter x:Name="PART_ContentPresenter"
                                                  Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                                  Margin="{Binding Padding, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}"
                                                  HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                                  VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                  TextElement.Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" />
                            </Border>
                        </Border>
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Setter Property="FocusAdorner">
                <FocusAdornerTemplate>
                    <Border BorderBrush="{DynamicResource FireAccentPale}"
                            BorderThickness="{StaticResource FireFocusRingThickness}"
                            Margin="{StaticResource FireFocusRingOffset}" />
                </FocusAdornerTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover /template/ Border#Sheen">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireSheenHover}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:pressed /template/ Border#Sheen">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireSheenPressed}" />
            </Style>
            <!-- Disabled is NEUTRAL, not a faded accent: 45 % blue with 45 %
                 ink read as blue on blue. -->
            <Style Selector="^:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireSurfaceChip}" />
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextDim}" />
            </Style>
            <!-- The rules below were global class styles until #240. They are LAST
                 so they still beat this theme's own setters, as a global style did. -->
            <Style Selector="^.Danger">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource DangerBg}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource DangerBorder}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource DangerColor}" />
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusSm}" />
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="18,10" />
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{StaticResource FontSizeMd}" />
                <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="36" />
                <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
                <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="scale(1.0)" />
                <Setter Property="Transitions">
                    <Transitions>
                        <BrushTransition Property="Background" Duration="0:0:0.15" />
                        <BrushTransition Property="BorderBrush" Duration="0:0:0.15" />
                        <TransformOperationsTransition Property="RenderTransform" Duration="0:0:0.08" />
                        <DoubleTransition Property="Opacity" Duration="0:0:0.15" />
                    </Transitions>
                </Setter>
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Danger:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource DangerHoverBg}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource DangerColor}" />
                <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource DangerColor}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Danger:pressed">
                <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="scale(0.97)" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Danger:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource DangerHoverBg}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource DangerColor}" />
                <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource DangerColor}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Danger:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.45" />
                <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Arrow" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Danger:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource DangerBg}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource DangerBorder}" />
                <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource DangerColor}" />
            </Style>
            <!-- #348: the shared Danger state rules above paint PART_ContentPresenter, which
                 is the whole button in Fluent's template but only the padded content strip
                 inside this one's lit fill, so hover and press drew a dark bar inside the
                 CTA. In this template the Sheen is the hover; the strip stays clear. A
                 separate rule, so the shared copies stay identical (ButtonControlThemeTests). -->
            <Style Selector="^.Danger:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter, ^.Danger:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter, ^.Danger:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Compact">
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="10,5" />
                <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="28" />
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{StaticResource FontSizeSm}" />
            </Style>
            <!-- The CTA at ROW scale. The hero spelling is sized for the front door's
                 "PLAY NOW" and the launch screen's "START" — one short word across a
                 wide button. In a 392 px rail or a modal footer, beside other actions,
                 its 28 px padding and display tracking make a two-word localized label
                 wider than the control that holds it. Same shape, same chamfer, same
                 glow; just not shouting. -->
            <Style Selector="^.FireCta.Compact">
                <Setter Property="Height" Value="{StaticResource FireButtonHeight}" />
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="18,0" />
            </Style>
            <!-- The CTA that DESTROYS something (a confirmation's "Delete"): the same
                 lit shape in the signal red, so it cannot read as the dialog's Save.
                 The ink stays FireTextOnAccent — dark on the light red, as on the blue.
                 A class style outranks the ControlTheme's own :disabled setter, so the
                 disabled state is restated here, neutral like every other lit action. -->
            <Style Selector="^.FireCta.Danger">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireDanger}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.FireCta.Danger:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireSurfaceChip}" />
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>

        <ControlTheme x:Key="FirePrimaryButton" TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentAction}" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextOnAccent}" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="{StaticResource FireActionHeight}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="30,0" />
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FireFontDisplay}" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{StaticResource FireWeightDisplay}" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{StaticResource FireSizeMd}" />
            <!-- .22em at 14 px. The port had 2.2 (.157em), below the spec's
                 .20-.24em band — a primary caption that is not conspicuously
                 tracked stops reading as a caption. -->
            <Setter Property="LetterSpacing" Value="{StaticResource FireTrackAction}" />
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
            <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translateY(0px)" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border x:CompileBindings="False"
                            Background="Transparent"
                            BoxShadow="{DynamicResource FireGlowAction}">
                        <Border x:Name="Cut"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusControl}"
                                fire:FireShape.CutSize="{StaticResource FireCutSize}">
                            <Border.Clip>
                                <!-- bounds AND the theme's cut: a converter parameter is a
                                     plain value, so the token has to arrive as a binding. -->
                                <MultiBinding Converter="{StaticResource FireChamferClip}">
                                    <Binding ElementName="Cut" Path="Bounds" />
                                    <Binding ElementName="Cut" Path="(fire:FireShape.CutSize)" />
                                </MultiBinding>
                            </Border.Clip>
                            <Border x:Name="Sheen" Background="Transparent">
                                <ContentPresenter x:Name="PART_ContentPresenter"
                                                  Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                                  Margin="{Binding Padding, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}"
                                                  HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                                  VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                  TextElement.Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" />
                            </Border>
                        </Border>
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Setter Property="FocusAdorner">
                <FocusAdornerTemplate>
                    <Border BorderBrush="{DynamicResource FireAccentPale}"
                            BorderThickness="{StaticResource FireFocusRingThickness}"
                            Margin="{StaticResource FireFocusRingOffset}" />
                </FocusAdornerTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover /template/ Border#Sheen">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireSheenHover}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:pressed /template/ Border#Sheen">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireSheenPressed}" />
            </Style>
            <!-- Disabled is NEUTRAL, not a faded accent: 45 % blue with 45 %
                 ink read as blue on blue. -->
            <Style Selector="^:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireSurfaceChip}" />
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextDim}" />
            </Style>
            <!-- The rules below were global class styles until #240. They are LAST
                 so they still beat this theme's own setters, as a global style did. -->
            <Style Selector="^.Primary">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource PrimaryGradient}" />
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextOnAccent}" />
                <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource RadiusSm}" />
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="20,10" />
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{StaticResource FontSizeMd}" />
                <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
                <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="36" />
                <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="scale(1.0)" />
                <Setter Property="Transitions">
                    <Transitions>
                        <BrushTransition Property="Background" Duration="0:0:0.15" />
                        <TransformOperationsTransition Property="RenderTransform" Duration="0:0:0.08" />
                        <DoubleTransition Property="Opacity" Duration="0:0:0.15" />
                    </Transitions>
                </Setter>
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Primary /template/ ContentPresenter">
                <Setter Property="BoxShadow" Value="0 0 0 0 Transparent" />
                <Setter Property="Transitions">
                    <Transitions>
                        <BoxShadowsTransition Property="BoxShadow" Duration="0:0:0.18" Easing="CubicEaseOut" />
                    </Transitions>
                </Setter>
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Primary:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource PrimaryGradientHover}" />
                <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextOnAccent}" />
                <Setter Property="BoxShadow" Value="0 0 0 0 Transparent" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Primary:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource PrimaryGradientHover}" />
                <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextOnAccent}" />
                <Setter Property="BoxShadow" Value="0 0 0 0 Transparent" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Primary:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.45" />
                <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Arrow" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^.Primary:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource SurfaceActive}" />
                <Setter Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextDim}" />
                <Setter Property="BoxShadow" Value="0 0 0 0 Transparent" />
            </Style>
            <!-- #348: as in FireCtaButton, the copied Primary state rules paint the padded
                 content strip inside this template's lit fill, a box behind the label on
                 hover and press. The Sheen is the hover here; the strip stays clear. -->
            <Style Selector="^.Primary:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter, ^.Primary:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter, ^.Primary:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            </Style>
            <!-- ══ THE PRIMARY ACTION'S CAPTION IS THE BODY FACE ════════════════════
                 `FirePrimaryButton` is Chakra Petch at `FireTrackAction` (.22em) —
                 the caption face — so "Design", "Match from audio", "Match all" and
                 "Apply as tone set" read as HEADINGS rather than as things to press.
                 `.Body` keeps the chamfer, the glow and the lift and swaps the face;
                 a class Style beats a ControlTheme setter, so nothing about the
                 template changes.

                 THE CHAMFER IS THE RULE FOR PRIMARY ACTIONS AND NOTHING ELSE (W4).
                 The rig used to mix four emphases — `FirePrimary` (chamfered),
                 `FireGhost.Accent` (rounded card, display face), `FireOutlineButton`
                 and `FireOutlineCta` — with no rule saying which was the primary. On
                 the tone surfaces there is exactly one chamfered button per block and
                 every other action is a framed `FireGhost`. -->
            <Style Selector="^.FirePrimary.Body">
                <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FireFontUi}" />
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{StaticResource FireWeightUi}" />
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{StaticResource FireSizeRow}" />
                <Setter Property="LetterSpacing" Value="0" />
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="20,0" />
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>

        <!-- ─── Segmented control — BUILT ONCE ───────────────────────────────
             One theme, reused by every segmented strip in the app: the
             Progress tab bar, snapshots, snap, routing, mic models, count-in.
             It had drifted into TWO implementations that restated the same
             look — a static `Border.FireSegmentItem` and a `ToggleButton`
             class style fighting Fluent's `:checked` setters through
             `/template/ ContentPresenter` — and the two disagreed: the big
             `.Tab` variant carried its own literal `#425E9FF2` (.26) fill and
             an 8 px item radius against the spec's .28 and 5-6 px.

             A `RadioButton` derives from `ToggleButton`, so the same theme
             drives both. Reach for the RadioButton when the strip is genuinely
             single-select (the spec's own note) and the ToggleButton when the
             screen already owns the mutual exclusion. -->
        <ControlTheme x:Key="FireSegmentItemToggle" TargetType="ToggleButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{StaticResource FireRadiusInner}" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="{StaticResource FirePadSegmentItem}" />
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FireFontMono}" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{StaticResource FireSizeMono}" />
            <Setter Property="LetterSpacing" Value="{StaticResource FireTrackStatus}" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextMuted}" />
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border x:Name="Fill" x:CompileBindings="False"
                            Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                            BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                            CornerRadius="{Binding CornerRadius, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}">
                        <ContentPresenter x:Name="PART_ContentPresenter"
                                          Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                          Margin="{Binding Padding, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}"
                                          HorizontalAlignment="{Binding HorizontalContentAlignment, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}}"
                                          VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                          TextElement.Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" />
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Setter Property="FocusAdorner">
                <FocusAdornerTemplate>
                    <Border BorderBrush="{DynamicResource FireAccentPale}"
                            BorderThickness="{StaticResource FireFocusRingThickness}"
                            Margin="-3"
                            CornerRadius="{StaticResource FireRadiusSegment}" />
                </FocusAdornerTemplate>
            </Setter>
            <Style Selector="^:pointerover">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireSurfaceHover}" />
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextBody}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:pressed">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentTintSoft}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:checked">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentTintStrong}" />
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource FireTextBright}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:checked:pointerover">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FireAccentTintStrong}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^:disabled">
                <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.45" />
            </Style>
            <!-- The BIG variant: Chakra captions instead of mono, a roomier
                 inset — but the SAME item radius and the same active fill. -->
            <Style Selector="^.Tab">
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="18,8" />
                <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource FireFontDisplay}" />
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{StaticResource FireWeightDisplay}" />
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{StaticResource FireSizeBase}" />
                <Setter Property="LetterSpacing" Value="1" />
            </Style>
            <!-- …and the DENSE spelling, for a strip that is narrower than the shared
                 `FirePadSegmentItem` (12,6) was drawn for. Get Ready's left rail is a
                 FIXED 404 px holding a 92 px label plus the strip, so its six-up speed
                 row gave each cell 17 px of content — "100" needs 22.8 and was sliced —
                 and its three-up chord row gave 58 for a "Standard" that needs 60.8.
                 Both were found by the UI sweep and sat on its `clipped-text` backlog.
                 A LOCAL override rather than a smaller shared token: every other
                 segmented strip in the app (the Progress tab bar, snapshots, snap,
                 routing, mic models, count-in) has the room and should keep the
                 breathing space. Vertical padding is untouched, so the strip's height
                 still matches every other one.

                 Spelled for BOTH element types, like `.Tab` above: the `:is(ToggleButton)`
                 selector really does reach a RadioButton at runtime, but
                 `FireClassReachabilityTests` reads the selectors LITERALLY, and without
                 the RadioButton spelling `Classes="FireSegmentItem Dense"` on one is
                 indistinguishable from a typo. -->
            <Style Selector="^.FireSegmentItem.Dense">
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="{StaticResource FirePadSegmentItemDense}" />
            </Style>
        </ControlTheme>
    </Styles.Resources>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         THE COMPONENT HALF, BY SECTION. Every `<Style>` this file used to
         declare inline now lives in `Styles/Fire/`, sliced along the section
         banners it already carried and moved byte for byte.

         ORDER IS THE CONTRACT, NOT A PREFERENCE. Avalonia applies styles in
         the order it walks this collection, so a later selector wins over an
         earlier one of equal specificity. These includes stand in the exact
         order the sections stood in the one file; a new section goes at the
         END unless it MEANS to override something above it.

         The `Styles.Resources` block above is deliberately NOT split.
         `FireChamferClip` is consumed by `FireCtaButton` and
         `FirePrimaryButton` through `{StaticResource}`, which resolves at
         parse time against what is already declared ABOVE it in the SAME
         dictionary — split those apart and the two chamfered buttons stop
         building, or worse, resolve to nothing. Keep that cluster whole.
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireGroundAndType.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireMarksAndMeters.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireInputs.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireActions.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireSectionsAndOverlays.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireRigBoard.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireRigUnitsAndGear.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireRigRolesAndTones.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireRigStage.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireRigHardware.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FirePopoverBody.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FirePopoverButtons.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireRigEditors.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireShellRail.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://DotCharter.Tone.UI/Styles/Fire/FireShellTitle.axaml" />

</Styles>
